{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792836267,"nonce":"/ciPTmkvbFz6lay4HF6i4wsTkbM=","title":"TypeScript: false rejections of library globals and unmodelled value forms","message":"Eleven official rows the reference accepts were rejected with type errors: library globals read as values (Date, JSON, Uint8Array, Atomics, Symbol called as a function) reported 'cannot find name'; `as const` reported 'unknown type const'; unary plus on a template string reported a number assignability error; a class in a .d.ts file was checked for property initialization; a source-phase import of ./a.wasm reported 'cannot resolve module'.\n\nTypeScript accepts unary + and - on any operand except possibly undefined ones, and every class in a declaration file is ambient. Plan: library globals not modelled natively, const assertions, numeric conversion of non-boolean operands, delete of a property, ambient classes in declaration files, and source or deferred import phases report Unsupported. Unary + and - on booleans convert through an integer. `delete` of an operand that is not a property reference is TypeScript's 2703.","files":null}]}